# `setp.lt.u32` compares unsigned. ptxas runs the first store on threads
# 16 to 47, %tid.x - 16 wrapping below 16, and the second on the
# threads with %tid.x mod 16 == 0, %tid.x << 28 wrapping above 15. An
# unsigned comparison is read only when both operands lie in [0, 2^32)
# on every thread, so both stores are bounds.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/setp_unsigned.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_setp_unsigned
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)  warp: <= 5 sectors (ideal <= 4)  [4 * %tid.x + param_0]
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 256 B
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_setp_unsigned_wraps
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)  warp: <= 5 sectors (ideal <= 4)  [4 * %tid.x + param_0]
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 256 B
